 their version of the 5700 xt ends up  performing on average about 25  better than buying a much cheaper  third-party card  where the same card under windows is far  more powerful and that is using opencl  which always scores lower than metal but  it gets  worse the w5700 that apple wants you to  buy  shipped with its own driver issues  causing consistent crashes and many  popular pro  apps and apple promised a fix back in  august  but it's been seven months and people  are still having the same  issue and amd even stated that it is an  issue with apple's drivers that they  can't  fix and apple needs to fix it and it's  been almost a year  since that graphics card launched and  lastly for graphics card  amd's powerful new 6000 series of  graphics cards that released four months  ago are still  not compatible with the mac pro with  users waiting on  each and each macos beta release to  hopefully get support  or for apple to release their version of  the card now i don't know about you  but this isn't what i was expecting when  i got this machine a year ago  sure it may have tons of ports for  upgrades but if apple is keeping  everything so locked down  and not working on bug fixes what is the  point for this machine  to be upgradable we also had a recent  report that amd may repurpose its apple  exclusive gpus into cryptocurrency  mining units  which makes it sound like apple may be  ditching amd altogether and moving  completely to its own graphics ships  and that's the only thing that can  explain why they are so behind on driver  updates  and new parts for their super expensive  pro  custom machine and now we know that  apple is working on a new mac pro that  will be about half the size and use  apple's cpus and gpus but deem did a  video on this and it will be an  absolute decent performance with really  good optimization  and most likely a lower price as well  bringing us back down to that starting  price of all the previous mac pros  once adjusted for inflation so with all  of that it seems like apple almost gave  up on the mac pro less than a year after  launch  and we know it's because apple silicon  macs are the future  even with the weakest mac mini which i  compared to this 50 000 mac pro  where it stood up to you and even beat  out the mac pro in many real world tests  apple knows that their own chips are the  future of max  and i think that is why they haven't  really been focusing on this mac pro  and thanks to our tests and comparisons  a lot of you guys know this as well  which is probably why i haven't been  able to sell my mac pro for over two  months now  even though it's priced at close to half  off nobody wants to buy it  and i don't blame them so what should  you buy if you need a powerful machine  and you can't wait for a new m1x mac  or apple silicon mac pro well if you're  looking for a new machine i think that  the 5k imac with the acor processor and  whichever graphics you need is a great  bang for the buck  or even better if you can find a used  imac  pro at a deep deep discount i think the  prices will stay  fairly well on those since they've  already been dropping so much  as soon as they've discontinued these  and of course they are not going to be  making  any new ones so that's going to keep the  value up now if you do  need pci slots or a bunch of gpu power  and you want to buy a mac pro  try to find a discounted used one like  mine instead of dropping 15 000 on a new  one  and then when you're ready to replace it  you will lose a lot less money  overall my question is why would apple  release this mac pro if they knew that  it would get slaughtered so  quickly after its release and by apple  itself  due to new cheaper faster machines and  then them basically seemingly giving up  working on it to me it is a huge bummer  and even though it still performs great  in many tasks  i can't help feel that even though apple  finally made another modular pro machine  it doesn't really matter now and apple  once again screwed the pros  but let me know your thoughts down below  is the mac pro still worth it  or should i have never been released  until apple was ready with their own  chips  go ahead and check out my comparison  with the m1 mac mini right over there  and click above to subscribe if you guys  want to see more videos like this one  this max and i'll see you in the next  [Music]  video


